      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.3,
          "end": 9.05,
          "en": "That's it for the basics of rest APIs, we'll dive much deeper into rest APIs and build a real project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 9.05,
          "end": 12.02,
          "en": "with the rest API in the next module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 12.08,
          "end": 14.54,
          "en": "The core concept and ideas are that rest",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.54,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "APIs are all about data, no user interface logic is exchanged. Rest APIs are normal node servers though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21.8,
          "end": 26.06,
          "en": "and that is really important to keep in mind, we're not building a totally different kind of app all of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 26.06,
          "end": 34.64,
          "en": "a sudden, just the data format and the way we send responses changes because now we simply expose a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 34.64,
          "end": 38.33,
          "en": "of endpoints which is a combination of http methods and paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 38.33,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "but we did this before too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 40.31,
          "end": 47.39,
          "en": "we just have more http methods available now and we exchange data in the json format for both requests and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 47.39,
          "end": 48.19,
          "en": "responses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 48.26,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "we don't return html pages as the response anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 51.97,
          "end": 56.78,
          "en": "Rest APIs are decoupled from the clients therefore, they are totally decoupled,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 56.78,
          "end": 61.83,
          "en": "they don't share any connection history or store any connection history.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 61.97,
          "end": 67.07,
          "en": "Now when we have a look at the requests and responses, it is important to understand that you should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 67.07,
          "end": 73.46000000000001,
          "en": "attach data for requests and responses in the json format and that you should let the other end know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 73.82,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "by setting the content type header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 76.53,
          "end": 80.45,
          "en": "Expressjs does this automatically when using the json method, in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 80.48,
          "end": 84.98,
          "en": "it depends on which method you use, when using the fetch API as we did,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 85.01,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "we had to set it manually, when you would use axios",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 88.24,
          "end": 93.3,
          "en": "another common library in browser side javascript for sending async requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 93.38,
          "end": 95.5,
          "en": "it would be done automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 98.50999999999999,
          "en": "Cors errors are also something we had to look at,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 98.50999999999999,
          "end": 104.87,
          "en": "they occur when the API and your client are sitting on different servers, different domains and they",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 104.87,
          "end": 106.28,
          "en": "want to exchange data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 106.28,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "You fix them in quotation marks because they are a security mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 110.6,
          "end": 117.53,
          "en": "but you can bypass that on purpose by setting the right cors headers which basically tell the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 117.71000000000001,
          "end": 119.18,
          "en": "hey it's fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 119.18,
          "end": 120.46,
          "en": "I'm a public API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 120.47,
          "end": 122.17,
          "en": "you may use my data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 122.33,
          "end": 124.13,
          "en": "These are the basics.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 124.13,
